From be996416d6c9667295017b68d0ed53bb7e254294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:30:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(machine): rigid tapping refused by name at the program
 gate, validated in the .mch

spindle.rigid_tapping is now a validated capability: anything but
true/false/null refuses the file by name at the reader (parse_mch) and
in the Machines pane's validator, instead of reading as "not limited".
The machine check (the gate every post path runs) refuses a path that
carries tap cycles on a machine stating false, naming the op and the
machine, whatever post is chosen - before, only tormach.cps read it, so
a 770M with the Fanuc or Haas post posted G84 silently. Never converted
to another cycle. The pane's Spindle row reads yes / no - tap cycles are
refused / not stated - not limited.

Every Tormach mill and router file states it (pinned); the lathes are
tracked in #795. Unstated stays "not limited", so other machines and
the 770MX G84 golden are unchanged. Decision: docs/decisions/786-rigid-tapping.md.

Fixes #786

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
